# Mini-BMAD (ad-hoc)

- When the user asks for **research**, **meeting planning**, **presentation brainstorming**, or other **ad-hoc** work they want to keep organized and summarizable, default to using `_mini_bmad/` runs.
- Create/open a run via `scripts/mini-bmad.ps1`:
  - `.\scripts\mini-bmad.ps1 new "<topic>"`
  - `.\scripts\mini-bmad.ps1 open "<run-slug>"`
- Keep all one-off artifacts inside the run folder (notes, agendas, outlines, links, decisions).
- Treat `_mini_bmad/runs/...` as **private by default** (gitignored). Do not publish raw runs unless the user explicitly wants to.
- If the user wants to share/publish outputs, copy curated artifacts into `Published/` (sanitized, minimal).
- While working, maintain an always-on **very short pending changes list** in the run:
  - `bmad run/.mini-bmad/CHANGES.md`
  - Add one bullet per meaningful event/item changed (new decision, new constraint, new agenda, key finding).
  - Do not clear this list during normal work.
- Use checkpoints to record where the user left off:
  - `.\scripts\mini-bmad.ps1 checkpoint "<run-slug>" -Step "<where you left off / next step>"`
- When the user is confident and wants to “wrap up”, generate a consolidated pack:
  - `.\scripts\mini-bmad.ps1 summarize "<run-slug>"`
- When the user says “Summarize my work from my last summary”, produce a **delta summary** (very short bullets) and clear pending changes:
  - `.\scripts\mini-bmad.ps1 delta "<run-slug>"`
- If you (the agent) make meaningful updates during a run, prefer logging them immediately:
  - `.\scripts\mini-bmad.ps1 log "<run-slug>" -Item "<short change>"`
- If the run should update a major BMAD project, link and sync:
  - `.\scripts\mini-bmad.ps1 link "<run-slug>" -Project "<bmad-project-slug>"`
  - `.\scripts\mini-bmad.ps1 summarize "<run-slug>" -Sync`
  - or sync only the delta:
    - `.\scripts\mini-bmad.ps1 delta "<run-slug>" -Sync`
  - Sync outputs land in `bmad-projects/<slug>/_mini-bmad-updates/` as import payloads the major project can incorporate.

